  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Small-Hours Observatory",
    "overview": "Oneiratory looks like a serious, faintly mystical corner of the web, kept by someone rigorous: a nocturnal observatory for dreams. Dusk-lavender paper under a barely-there starfield, thin panels with softly rounded corners, a full-width dusty-indigo header, serif headings, and calm system-sans prose. It reads as an instrument someone has been quietly running in the small hours, keeping an honest record; the wonder is real, the presentation disciplined. One unified system across every page (shared oneiratory.css), with two moods split by purpose: the serious Instrument and the looser Commons board, sharing one palette and chrome.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One shared system across all pages: dusk-lavender paper, faint starfield, softly-rounded (9px) panels, a full-width sticky indigo header, calm system-sans prose.",
      "Two moods by purpose: the serious Instrument and the looser Commons board, sharing one palette and chrome.",
      "'Faint' lives in the chrome (borders, counts, meta); reading text and hit/miss labels stay fully legible.",
      "Evidence over persuasion: the homepage demonstrates the seal and shows hits beside honest misses.",
      "Georgia (headings) + system-sans (prose) + monospace (exact values). One restrained terracotta accent. No gradients, no glass, no glow."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The No-Glow Rule",
        "body": "No gradients, no backdrop-filter, no glass, no pill buttons, no drop-shadow glows. Flat fills, softly rounded corners (6-9px), 1px borders. The instant something looks glossy it reads as AI, the one thing this system may never do.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One-Accent Rule",
        "body": "Terracotta (--warm) is the only warm colour and appears only on primary actions and small leading marks. Structure is violet/indigo; warmth is the accent. Do not introduce a second accent hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Truth-Signal Rule",
        "body": "Sage means hit, mauve means miss, seal indigo means sealed-and-waiting. Never decorative (sage doubles only as Commons greentext).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Machine-Voice Rule",
        "body": "Anything literally exact (a hash, timestamp, seal ID, declared condition, post number, stat) is monospace.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif-For-Wonder Rule",
        "body": "Georgia is reserved for the wordmark, hero, headings, leads, and awed lines; never UI chrome or dense body text.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Rule",
        "body": "Depth is a 1px line and a flat fill, never a shadow. Corners are softly rounded (6-9px), not sharp and not fully round.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Starfield-Is-Background Rule",
        "body": "The faint dot texture lives in the fixed body background only. It never overlaps or dims content, and stays under ~0.2 alpha so it reads as dusk, not decoration.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep everything on the one shared system: link oneiratory.css, use the .site-header, .cap/.in panels, .btn/.btn-primary/.btn-ghost, and .site-footer.",
      "Do keep every surface flat: 1px hairlines, flat fills, 6-9px corners.",
      "Do reserve terracotta for primary actions and small leading marks only.",
      "Do set every exact value in monospace and reserve Georgia for the wordmark, hero, headings, leads, and awed asides.",
      "Do reserve sage/mauve/seal-indigo for hit/miss/sealed.",
      "Do spend 'faint' on chrome; keep reading text at --ink and hit/miss labels fully legible.",
      "Do let the Commons keep its board character while sharing the site's header, type, tokens, and footer."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't ever reintroduce the AI look: no gradient-filled pills, no backdrop-filter/glass, no pastel radial-gradient washes, no glossy dreamcore, no uppercase eyebrow on every section.",
      "Don't give a page its own palette or its own header/footer. If it looks like a different site, it is wrong.",
      "Don't use a coloured side-stripe (border-left/right > 1px as an accent) on cards, replies, or callouts.",
      "Don't bring back Verdana or the Windows-9x button bevel.",
      "Don't drift into psychic/occult woo or crypto/web3 hype.",
